text:
claire: Quick FYI  we're opening a limited preview for a new inference-focused SKU, Aurora-Edge, in ca-central (Toronto) and eu-west-2 (Copenhagen). Target: ultra-low tail latency for regional LLM endpoints and proxy frontends. Reservations open 2026-08-18 04:00 UTC via Console + API. :sparkles;
hao: Is Aurora-Edge new hardware or a tuned profile? headline perf?;
mike: Tuned profile of Aurora line with smaller working-set and altered interconnect for fast small-batch inference. Early p50 ~30ms, p95 ~110ms on 4k context int8 with per-request affinity. We'll publish full bench later.;
claire: SLA: 99.9% reserved availability during preview. Burst policy: up to 12% of pool for 3m windows, 3x/day. Bursts will be limited first 48h while we calibrate.;
ops-bot: Initial fleet: ca-central = 36 units (9 clusters), eu-west-2 = 24 units (6 clusters). Per-org preview cap: 8 units.;
deploy-bot: Rollout plan: canary -> 20% -> 60% -> GA. Canary starts 2026-08-18 04:00 UTC. Extra tracing enabled for 72h.;
hao: Migration path for existing Aurora reserved customers?;
claire: Migration offer: prorated credit + 45d overlap for active Aurora reservations. Submit migration interest: https://intra.redwood.io/dedicated/migrate-aurora (internal).;
billing: Preview reservations use sku aurora-edge.preview and are not billed until conversion or GA opt-in. Conversion offers include prorated credits for active commitments. Contact billing@redwood.com for quotes.;
mike: API example (internal):
```
curl -X POST https://api.redwood.internal/v1/dedicated/reservations \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"region":"ca-central","gpu_type":"aurora-edge","units":2,"term_months":6}'
```;
partners: Quota expand timeline for partners?;
ops-bot: Request via Console > Support > Dedicated quotas. Preview expansions typically 24-72h.;
claire: I'll host a 25m office hours tomorrow 15:00 BST in #dedicated to walk through reservation flow and migration details. Ping me if you want a demo slot. :calendar:
